{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And brightness</b> — that which went forth from before Him was like light; this was like a pillar of fire." "<b>And horns</b> — like: \"because the skin of Moses' face was horned\" (Exodus 34:29)." "<b>And there is the hiding of His might</b> — this is the Ark, like: \"you and the ark of your might\" (1 Samuel 4:3). And it is written: \"for the cloud of YHWH was upon the tabernacle by day, and fire was in it by night\" (Exodus 40:38), and the yod of חביון is in place of an alef." "And the meaning of <b>חביון עזו</b> is the Ark, which was hidden and concealed and covered when they carried it. Or it belongs to those who use the heh [as a root letter], like: \"my hiding is almost a moment until wrath passes\" (Isaiah 26:20)."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:13.027312598Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}